why: the fact that a posting reference puts a semicolon before each qualifier is why the cells are joined with a newline, and run 13's writer said so in its own restatement but wrote the fact and the join as two sentences with no tie; where the fact rules out an alternative the act avoids, the act names it Rescored 2026-09-29 under §94: subject and phrasing keeps dropped, so its column no longer compares.
labelled: 2026-09-28
--- code
export function formatPostingIdentities(identity: PostingIdentity): string {
  return [identity.book, identity.reference, identity.settlementHost].join('\n');
}
--- facts
A posting reference puts a semicolon before each of its qualifiers, such as the clearing list.
